      "id": "claim_d8dfcbcd8158460a9de12ca4ed385240",
      "statement": "On a bound volume's arrival, the removable coordinator rebuilds each folder path from the mount path and stored relative path, remaps changed persisted paths, reconciles watching, resets failed work below the folder, and triggers a scan. On removal it clears the active-volume entry, emits a removal event, and unwatches bound folders without deleting their rows. Windows supplies removable-drive device events, while the macOS and Linux monitor implementations are no-ops.",
